   "memo": "<ul><li><strong>Fact table [1]:</strong> stores numeric, additive measures such as sales amount, quantity and cost, plus foreign keys to dimensions.</li><li><strong>Dimension table [1]:</strong> stores descriptive attributes such as product, customer, time and region that provide the &ldquo;by what&rdquo; context for analysis.</li><li><strong>Star schema [1]:</strong> one central fact table joined directly to denormalised dimension tables, giving fewer joins and fast queries.</li><li><strong>Snowflake schema [1]:</strong> dimensions are normalised into multiple related tables, reducing redundancy but increasing the number of joins.</li><li><strong>Trade-off [1]:</strong> star schemas favour query simplicity and speed; snowflake schemas favour storage efficiency and structural rigour at the cost of complexity.</li></ul>",
